From: binsquare <hebinsquared@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tsi: report Linux IPv4 UDP family errors

Reject unsupported IPv4 UDP destination families with EAFNOSUPPORT
without changing the existing peer, matching native Linux behavior.

Signed-off-by: binsquare <hebinsquared@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/tsi/af_tsi.c
+++ b/net/tsi/af_tsi.c
@@ -677,6 +677,11 @@
 			"%s: rejecting mismatched family addr->sa_family=%d tsk->family=%d\n",
 			__func__, addr->sa_family, tsk->family);
 		err = -EINVAL;
+		/* Match the IPv4 UDP stack without changing the current peer. */
+		if (tsi_host_enabled(tsk) && sk->sk_type == SOCK_DGRAM &&
+		    tsk->family == AF_INET && addr->sa_family != AF_UNSPEC &&
+		    addr_len >= sizeof(struct sockaddr_in))
+			err = -EAFNOSUPPORT;
 		goto release;
 	}
 
